Here are CODEOWNERS suggestions based on blame at HEAD. Ownership is shown only where one person holds at least half of the surviving non-bot lines.

```
# Suggested CODEOWNERS. Owners are listed only where one person holds >= 50% of surviving lines.
/lib/           <email redacted>     # 150 of 238 lines (63.0%)
/test/          <email redacted>     # 486 of 966 lines (50.3%); margin is 3 lines
/.eslintrc.yml  <email redacted>  # 7 of 7 lines (100%)
/.gitignore     <email redacted>  # 4 of 5 lines (80%)
/HISTORY.md     <email redacted>  # 50 of 64 lines (78%)
/LICENSE        <email redacted>  # 17 of 22 lines (77%)
/package.json   <email redacted>  # 20 of 40 lines (50%), exactly at threshold
```

Where nobody reaches half:

- **`.github/`**: no owner. Top is Douglas Christopher Wilson at 108 of 366 (29.5%), then Íñigo Marquínez Prado at 25.7%.
- **Root files, pooled**: no owner. Top is Troy Goode at 122 of 415 (29.4%).
- **`README.md`**: no owner. Troy Goode holds 104 of 277 (37.5%).

The email addresses are placeholders. CODEOWNERS needs either a GitHub `@handle` or an email verified on a GitHub account, so substitute the handles if you prefer those.

Method:
- I ran `git blame` on HEAD and tallied the author of each surviving line.
- Fiona Formatter's `62628c0` reformatted 1,016 lines (indentation and quotes), so `git blame --ignore-rev` could not skip it. I attributed each line it touched back to its pre-reformat author, matching lines after normalizing whitespace and quotes.
- Bot lines (dependabot) are excluded from both the count and the total.
- Identities are merged for Troy Goode (`<email redacted>` and `troy@laptop.example`) and for Alejandro Caravaca Puchades (same email as the `alex94puchades` name).
- Blank lines count as lines.

The `/test/` and `package.json` owners are at the threshold, so they would flip if the line counting changed. I haven't written the CODEOWNERS file or committed anything. The tally script is in `/tmp/codeowners-scan/scan.py`, outside the repo.
